46388:150097","promptId":"#GZ1DZ","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":146388,"endPos":150097,"startLine":3596,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":3664,"endLineOffset":5,"length":3710}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":381,"start_side":"LEFT","start_line":379,"line":381,"comment_lines":["[379][]","[380][]","[381][]"],"review_comment":["`| stats c \u003d count(), call \u003d count(*), c_literal \u003d count(1)`  produced an `EsStatsQueryExec` that wasn\u0027t plannable by the LocalExecutionPlanner (`EsStatsQuery currently supports only one field statistic`).\r\n\r\nI think a way to properly fix this is:\r\n- normalize `count(*), count(1), count(), count(\"foobar\")` all to `count(*)` as part of surrogate substitution\r\n- deduplicate the counts - this requires refactoring `SubstituteExpressions` as its deduplication doesn\u0027t currently work well enough for this approach, and there\u0027s overlap with the deduplication happening in `ReplaceStatsAggExpressionWithEval`.","Once the count normalization happens, the deduplication should kick in (since all counts will be the same) and this type of query should work.\r\nThe critical bit here is normalization so count(*), count(1), count(), count(*) and count(1+1+2) all fold back to the same expression of count(1)."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","id":37859,"created_at":"2024-04-17T10:39:47Z","original_position":21,"side":"LEFT","position":21,"original_start_line":379,"submitted_on_commit":"7706d5f844f1ee0ddc4e694b36df1e052bab09ee","diff_hunk":"@@ -370,42 +370,17 @@ public void testAnotherCountAllWithFilter() {\n         assertThat(expected.toString(), is(esStatsQuery.query().t